Every agent now gets its own read record, so #1094 items 3 and 4 are closed. Item 1 is still open, so the commit says "Part of #1094" rather than "Fixes". Committed as 421f3b86; build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings, the format check and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

What changed
• `src/tools.rs`: the main agent's tools and each sub-agent's tools now create their own yoagent ReadLog, shared only by that agent's read_file and write_file.
  • The only other places that build these tools are a test-only helper and two existing test files, so I left them alone.
• Item 3: a sub-agent reading a file whole no longer lets the main agent overwrite a file it only read part of.
• Item 4: if a file changes on disk after a partial read (for example bash shrinks it), write_file refuses until that agent reads it whole again.
• yoyo's own guard still runs. ReadLog counts a page as read before yoyo cuts long output, so on its own it would undo the Day 242 fix for item 2. A write now has to pass both checks.

One change outside the plan: the plan said to only note this on the ticket, but I fixed it because users would pay for it. yoagent's refusal message wasn't recognised by prompt_retry::is_deterministic_tool_error, so a turn ending on that refusal would have been auto-retried several times. I added tools::READ_LOG_REFUSAL_STEM, a copy of yoagent's wording, plus a one-line check in src/prompt_retry.rs. A test compares it with the real refusal text, so if yoagent changes the wording the test fails.

Tests (src/tools_read_log_tests.rs, 6 tests on the real tool setup, temp dirs only)
• They cover items 3 and 4, the refusal wording, a whole-read-then-write case and a sub-agent write (both allowed), and never_read_overwrite_is_still_allowed_item_1_undecided.
• Positive controls, each removed and put back in one command:
  • Removing the read log from the main agent's write_file made exactly the item-3, item-4 and wording tests fail (3 of 6).
  • Removing the prompt_retry line made only the wording test fail.
  • After restoring, all 6 pass.
• I didn't run these tests on the code before my change, which the plan asked for. The first positive control is the closest I have: it removes the parent-side check those tests depend on.

Docs and records
• docs/src/troubleshooting/safety.md now says each agent and sub-agent has its own read record and explains the changed-on-disk refusal.
• I also updated the stale comment in src/partial_read_guard.rs, added an ARCHITECTURE.md entry, and updated the size limits in tests/module_size.rs (tools.rs 5247 → 5295, prompt_retry.rs +1).
• I posted the scope comment on #1094.

Known limits:
• A sub-agent's read record lasts across every time that sub-agent tool is called, not just one call.
• Rebuilding the main agent starts it with a fresh read record. yoyo's own guard still covers that gap.

